{"_id":"68a736128ec3d8323af14990","roadmapSlug":"data-analyst","nodeId":"ict4JkoVM-AzPbp9bDztg","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:06:58.099Z","description":"# Variance\n\nVariance measures the average squared deviation of each value from the mean. It quantifies how much the data points differ from the average. A higher variance indicates greater spread. Variance is the basis for standard deviation and many inferential statistical tests.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"What is Variance?","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/v/variance.asp","_id":"6a7f4a4fcb44947debcf5a94"},{"type":"article","title":"How to Calculate Variance","url":"https://www.scribbr.co.uk/stats/variance-meaning/","_id":"6a7f4a4fcb44947debcf5a95"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:03:11.488Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a8894ecaca636c6b9e973f1","title":"DataCamp - Associate Data Analyst in SQL","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/1GK1qD"},{"_id":"6a5e04dcfb5fcb94d041675b","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/AgYmJK"},{"_id":"6a5e189a077863512aba4c73","title":"roadmap.sh - Master SQL","partner":"roadmap.sh","type":"course","url":"https://roadmap.sh/courses/sql"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/data-analyst/content/ict4JkoVM-AzPbp9bDztg.md"}